{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwkAFQjSMCCmMXpng2wA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing in this repo has changed. Last time I only explained the cause and didn't edit anything, so if you were expecting a fix to land here, none did.\n\nI just checked the library itself. `slugify` gives dashes whenever it's passed `delim='-'`:\n\n- `'Hello World'` → `hello-world`\n- `'hello_world'` → `hello-world` (existing underscores get converted too)\n- `'Hello_World page'` → `hello-world-page`\n\nSo boltons isn't what's breaking. The underscores are coming from your site's code, and that code isn't in this repo. Most likely one of these:\n\n1. The call that builds the title still uses plain `slugify(title)` without `delim='-'`. There may be more than one such call.\n2. The site is running a different boltons install than this checkout, so edits here never reach it.\n3. The slugs were generated once and cached or saved, so old pages keep their `hello_world` names until they're regenerated.\n\nSend me the path to your site's repo, or the file that builds the page titles, and I'll find the call and fix it there. It would also help to have one title you typed in and the slug you're getting for it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":769,"cache_read_input_tokens":45731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":769},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8df62805-53f3-414b-a2ba-230310b5236c","uuid":"8c56900b-0cac-46ca-b6d3-f0489c0af988","timestamp":"2026-11-11T20:08:01.978Z","request_id":"req_011CgwkAFEZhnEx1HjHaxKrX"}
